{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Righteousness.</b> HaShem: 'Righteousness will walk before Him' — by way of metaphor. The correct interpretation: צדק is a noun and the word איש is missing, as though written: איש צדק לפניו." "<b>Will walk.</b> HaShem: 'as your fathers walked before Him, Abraham and Isaac.' The meaning: that a righteous man may be helped to walk before Him; and איש is missing, like: אל תהי מרי ואני תפלה (Jeremiah 15:10); צדק ישרת אחר (Isaiah 5:23); and so it is: ישם לדרך צדק פעמיו (Psalms 85:13). And behold, the meaning is doubled."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 85, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:08.319203826Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}